# Pin LF in both the index and the working tree. This clone currently relies on a
# local `core.autocrlf=input` to keep its CRLF working files from showing up as a
# tree full of phantom modifications — but that setting lives in .git/config, so it
# protects THIS clone only. A fresh clone, or a checkout on Windows, gets no such
# help. Committing the rule makes the fix travel with the repo.
#
# `text=auto` still detects binary content, so the tracked token art is untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff2 binary
